  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is the time period of simple pendulum on the earth&#39;s surface. Its time period becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></math> when taken to a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> (equal to earth&#39;s radius) above the earth&#39;s surface. Then, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Time period of a simple pendulum at Earth&#39;s surface is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>.</p><p>When distance from centre of Earth, i.e.,&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, acceleration due to gravity is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, time period is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}